  "notes": "{開幕|かいまく} literally means 'opening the curtain' ({開|かい} open + {幕|まく} curtain). Originally a theater term, it now commonly refers to the start of sports seasons and major events.\n\nUSAGE:\nUsed as a suru-verb: {開幕|かいまく}する (to open, to begin). The subject is typically an event or season, not a person.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {開幕|かいまく}{戦|せん} (opening game)\n- {開幕|かいまく}{投手|とうしゅ} (opening day pitcher)\n- シーズン{開幕|かいまく} (season opener)\n- {開幕|かいまく}ダッシュ (strong start to a season)\n- {開幕|かいまく}を{飾|かざ}る (to mark the opening)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {閉幕|へいまく}: closing (opposite)\n- {開会|かいかい}: opening of a meeting or ceremony (more formal, official)\n- {開始|かいし}: start, beginning (general-purpose)",
